# SYNOPSIS

```ndb
slot=a release=N tree=b2:HASH kernel=HEX svcd=HEX ktest=HEX bootfs=HEX
boot=a previous=- cmdline="WORDS"
```

# DESCRIPTION

An installed system's ESP has three boot slots, the directories `\EFI\vectra\a`, `b` and `c`.
Each holds one release's `kernel.elf`, the root task's modules `svcd` and `ktest`, and `bootfs.tar`.
The slot table, `\EFI\vectra\slots.ndb`, says what each slot holds, which slot boots, and which booted before it.
It is ndb text (see ndb(6)): a record for each slot in use, then one record for the table.

install(8) writes it with slot `a` in use and booting.
distd(8) reads it for its `status`, and rewrites it at `apply`, which fills a slot other than the one running and makes it the one that boots, and at `rollback`, which makes the previous slot boot again.
Both read and write it with `lib/vx-slots`, and each time they write it they write Limine's configuration, `\boot\limine\limine.conf`, from it alone, the table first, so the two never disagree.
There is one Limine, at the firmware's fallback path `\EFI\BOOT\BOOTX64.EFI` or `BOOTAA64.EFI`, and no UEFI boot entries: choosing a slot is rewriting the configuration.

A table is refused if it is not ndb, if it has a key not defined below, if it names no slot that boots, or if the slot that boots is not in use.
A slot is in use when its record has a `release` and all four file hashes; a record without them is read as a slot not in use.

## A slot

: `slot`
  The slot: `a`, `b` or `c`.
  A record whose `slot` is anything else is read as the table's record.
: `release`
  The number of the release in the slot, decimal (see release(6)).
  distd's `status` shows it as `current=` for the slot that booted and `boot=` for the slot that will.
: `tree`
  The release's base tree, `b2:` and 64 hex digits (see store(6)).
  Written, but not read; a longer value is cut to 67 characters.
: `kernel`, `svcd`, `ktest`, `bootfs`
  The BLAKE2b-512 hashes of the slot's `kernel.elf`, `svcd`, `ktest` and `bootfs.tar`, 128 hex digits each.
  install and distd compute them from the bytes as written to the ESP, distd reading each file back to be sure; they go into Limine's configuration, and Limine refuses a file that does not match.
  A value of another length leaves the slot not in use; one of the right length is not checked further.

## The table

: `boot`
  The slot that boots next: `a`, `b` or `c`.
  Required.
: `previous`
  The slot that booted before it, the one `rollback` returns to, or `-` for none.
  A slot not in use, and any other value, is read as none.
: `cmdline`
  The words each entry's kernel command line has after `vx.system vx.slot=`<x>: install writes the live system's command line without `vx.live`.
  Up to 255 bytes are kept; it may be empty, and the key may be left out.

When more than one record carries `boot`, `previous` or `cmdline`, the last that has a valid value is taken.
distd and install always write all three.

## Limine's configuration

The configuration is made from the table and has, after a comment saying so, `timeout: 0` and a `default_entry` naming the slot that boots, then an entry for each slot in use, in the order `a`, `b`, `c`.
An entry is titled `VectraOS (slot `<x>`, release `<n>`)`, uses Limine's own protocol, and names the slot's kernel by `path` and its three modules by `module_path`, each as `boot():/EFI/vectra/`<x>`/`<file> followed by `#` and the file's hash.
Its command line is `vx.system vx.slot=`<x>, then the table's `cmdline`.
`vx.system` starts the installed system's services (see svcd(8)); distd reads `vx.slot=` to know which slot booted.

# EXAMPLES

The table after the slots test has applied release 2 and rolled back, read from its disk with `mtype`, each 128-digit hash shortened here to its first and last eight:

```ndb
slot=a release=1
    tree=b2:3737dbc03157d82bf47af1d28851e7a57f41a1d80c4e9852ef6347f6e9f5538d
    kernel=2e524875…f23f09c6 svcd=ef2ed0a2…7b82cfe2
    ktest=59daa7e8…15410802 bootfs=ea125654…b68f895d
slot=b release=2
    tree=b2:b1defffc300df1104dda8d0a913de210b60472203846ae5f0d4292f136bc8b70
    kernel=2e524875…f23f09c6 svcd=ef2ed0a2…7b82cfe2
    ktest=59daa7e8…15410802 bootfs=351ce9c2…014ce040
boot=a previous=b cmdline=vx.skip=rc
```

and the configuration made from it, its hashes shortened in the same way, its comment cut short and its second entry left out:

```text
# Written from \EFI\vectra\slots.ndb (install, distd: M5 step 9). One entry
...
timeout: 0
default_entry: 1

/VectraOS (slot a, release 1)
    protocol: limine
    path: boot():/EFI/vectra/a/kernel.elf#2e524875…f23f09c6
    module_path: boot():/EFI/vectra/a/svcd#ef2ed0a2…7b82cfe2
    module_path: boot():/EFI/vectra/a/ktest#59daa7e8…15410802
    module_path: boot():/EFI/vectra/a/bootfs.tar#ea125654…b68f895d
    cmdline: vx.system vx.slot=a vx.skip=rc

/VectraOS (slot b, release 2)
...
```

# FILES

: `\EFI\vectra\slots.ndb`
  The slot table: `/tmp/EFI/vectra/slots.ndb` in distd's namespace, where the ESP is mounted.
: `\EFI\vectra\a`, `\EFI\vectra\b`, `\EFI\vectra\c`
  The slots.
: `\boot\limine\limine.conf`
  Limine's configuration, made from the table.

